{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And for that the dream was doubled unto Pharaoh twice</b>. The reason the dream was repeated twice in a single night is that it would have been possible for him to see in a single dream both the cows and the ears of grain, to inform him that there would be no plowing and harvest. But He made of it two dreams coming one after the other in a single night — and this is not the way of dreamers — to inform him that the matter is determined and Elohim is hastening to do it. This is the meaning of \"twice\" — for it was not repeated in a single instance. And Rabbi Abraham [Ibn Ezra] explains that the doubling of the dream in cows and in ears of grain is testimony that the matter is certain and established, but the fact that it was twice in a single night is testimony that Elohim is hastening to do it. If so, it should have been said that the ears of grain alone would have sufficed, since it is they that inform of the famine."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:43:31.340480608Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}